# Code owners for the legal dataset and the letters a worker actually sends.
#
# This file exists because of one failure mode: a well-meaning contributor updates a
# country's transposition status from a social-media post, a maintainer merges it on a
# Friday, and a worker sends a letter to their employer citing a law that was never
# enacted. The letter has already been sent. There is no reputational recovery path as
# cheap as prevention.
#
# Pair this file with branch protection on the default branch requiring ALL THREE named
# checks from `.github/workflows/legal-data.yml`:
#
#   - schema-and-lint
#   - offline-suite
#   - freshness-gate
#
# and with AUTO-MERGE DISABLED. No path below may be merged by automation alone, and
# there is no trusted-contributor carve-out on the two-person rule for a status or a
# deadline change. A pull request touching `country-data` with a green CI and one
# approving review from a bot is the exact shape this file exists to stop.

# Everything, as the backstop.
*                                   @MarekFish93

# The legal dataset. A change here decides what a worker cites to their employer.
/packages/country-data/             @MarekFish93
/packages/country-data/data/        @MarekFish93
/packages/country-data/proposed/    @MarekFish93

# The letter templates. Authored in Phase 5; the ownership is declared NOW so the phase
# inherits it rather than adding it late, when "we'll add CODEOWNERS after launch" has
# already become "we launched without CODEOWNERS".
/packages/letters/                  @MarekFish93

# The gates themselves. A pull request that weakens a byte floor, broadens an anchor,
# relaxes a lint rule or removes a required check must be reviewed as carefully as a
# change to the data it protects — more carefully, because it is invisible in the data.
/.github/workflows/                 @MarekFish93
